  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Hey! How's everything going?",
   "est_sec": 1.34,
   "gap_before": 0.5,
   "role": "greeting",
   "phrasing": "greet_07"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Hanging in there.",
   "est_sec": 1.03,
   "gap_before": 0.31,
   "event": "greeting_answer",
   "phrasing": "greet_ans_14"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Speed reading. Real or a scam?",
   "est_sec": 1.96,
   "gap_before": 0.45,
   "event": "ordinary_request",
   "block": "books.dlg11"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Mostly oversold. You can get somewhat faster with practice, but reading really fast usually means understanding less.",
   "est_sec": 5.37,
   "gap_before": 0.35,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "books.dlg11"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "So those apps that flash one word at a time?",
   "est_sec": 3.2,
   "gap_before": 0.5,
   "event": "ordinary_request",
   "block": "books.dlg11"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "They can help with simple text, but they make it hard to go back and reread, which is how we actually understand tricky parts.",
   "est_sec": 7.54,
   "gap_before": 1.74,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "books.dlg11"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "I just want to get through more books.",
   "est_sec": 2.58,
   "gap_before": 0.39,
   "event": "ordinary_request",
   "block": "books.dlg11"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Then the honest trick is more reading time, not faster reading. And letting yourself skim the boring bits.",
   "est_sec": 5.68,
   "gap_before": 0.65,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "books.dlg11"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Boring. But fair.",
   "est_sec": 1.03,
   "gap_before": 1.44,
   "event": "ordinary_request",
   "block": "books.dlg11"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "I know. The good news is that people who read a lot do naturally get faster over time.",
   "est_sec": 5.68,
   "gap_before": 0.96,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "books.dlg11"
  }
